    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ee58362_2f439259",
        "filename": "core/minute-ia/irq_handler.h",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-18T23:36:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why are we doing all this work here? I feel like we should just be jmp\u0027ing to the epilogue that is common code. We\u0027re consuming all thee bytes for each instance of DECLARE_IRQ_ usage.\n\nI would expect the sequence to be:\n\npusha\nadd $1, __in_isr\npush $irq_epilogue\njmp #routine\n\n\nin switch.S:\n\n.global irq_epilogue\nirq_epilogue:\npush $0\npush $0\ncall switch_handler\naddl $0x08, %esp\ntest %eax, %eax\njz 1f\n...\npopa\niret\n\nit could be broken up more, but currently you are duplicating many code paths that are the same in both switch.S and here. I don\u0027t understand why all of this duplicated.",
      "revId": "89c0db804b190c6293cc3651a29e6b9855db6b76",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eb860c3c_431e73b8",
        "filename": "core/minute-ia/irq_handler.h",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1127214
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-20T23:12:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We will investigate how to. \nEven if lines of code are duplicated from __switchto, there is difference.\n__swichto is handling SW interrupt which is only related to IOAPIC but DECLARE_IRQ is handling device interrupt whose interrupt path has additional IOAPIC specified by \u0027vector\u0027 and IOAPIC EIO should be cleared at the end(\"movl $\"#vector \", (0xFEC00040)\\n\") and due to this, it was hard to\nreuse code in __switchto. If we have to develop new common shared code, this code should receive \u0027vector\u0027 and flag for either SW IRQ or not as parameters.  This is why we copied code to DECLARE_IRQ.   \n\nFrom comment, I think you want to save FPU context every IRQ and assuming IRQ can use FP operation. Am I understanding correct ?\nFrom cortex-M code, ARM does not save FPU context every IRQ and save only when there is task switch to new task.",
      "parentUuid": "7ee58362_2f439259",
      "revId": "89c0db804b190c6293cc3651a29e6b9855db6b76",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e234efe_289f4d14",
        "filename": "core/minute-ia/irq_handler.h",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-21T22:28:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For the vast majority of the sequence the instructions are the same. Putting all this in a macro will make it such that every invocation will duplicate the instruction stream instead of reusing it. It\u0027s your call, but I think the code duplication is leading to divergence (this CL) as well as unnecessary program size bloat.",
      "parentUuid": "eb860c3c_431e73b8",
      "revId": "89c0db804b190c6293cc3651a29e6b9855db6b76",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
